IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mair-dates`
IMPORT `mair-core`
IMPORT `mair-seat`

-- Motor Accident Insurance Regulation 2018 (Qld) -- cases from the seat of the claimant. Every expected value is worked
-- by hand from the deposited text (sl-2018-0113, version in force from 1 July 2026), with the working in the comment
-- above it. Every exported question in mair-seat.l4 has cases, edges included.
--
-- A breached DEONTIC cannot be asserted with EQUALS on the stable l4, so the s 22 rule is asserted through CONSIDER
-- ... WHEN FULFILLED; the #TRACEs at the end carry an "expect:" line that was read.
--
-- The s 100A figures in the s 29 cases (lower offer limit $30,000, upper offer limit $50,000, declared costs limit
-- $3,500) are HYPOTHETICAL: the Minister's figures are not deposited.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases`

§§ `s 14 -- motorised mobility devices`

-- s 14(1): motorised mobility devices are gratuitously insured by the Nominal Defendant.
#ASSERT `Is the mobility device insured by the Nominal Defendant` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Nominal Defendant provides gratuitous insurance for motorised mobility devices (s 14)`
-- Any other vehicle: s 14 is silent.
#ASSERT `Is the mobility device insured by the Nominal Defendant` FALSE EQUALS `s 14 does not say: it covers only motorised mobility devices`

§§ `s 17 and s 19 -- what the notice must include`

-- Fullest case: own claim, employed, a passenger, a property damage claim made, consulted a lawyer, retained a law
-- practice. Of the 15 items, the two "plain" variants of (a)(iv) and (b)(iv) drop out: 13.
#ASSERT count (`What must my notice of claim include` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 13
#ASSERT elem "s 17(1)(a)(iv): your occupation and your employer's name and address" (`What must my notice of claim include` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT elem "s 17(1)(b)(iv): the injured person's, and the driver's, alcohol or drug consumption in the 12 hours before the accident" (`What must my notice of claim include` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT elem "s 17(1)(p): the date a doctor first physically examined you for the injury, the date the certifying doctor first did, and the certifying doctor's unique identifier" (`What must my notice of claim include` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Leanest case: a derivative claim, not employed, the injured person was the driver, no property claim, no lawyer: the
-- always-items (a), (b), (c)-(f)/(h)-(i), (j)-(o), 2(a), 2(b), s 19 = 7, plus plain occupation and plain alcohol = 9;
-- no (g), (p), (q), (r).
#ASSERT count (`What must my notice of claim include` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 9
#ASSERT (NOT (elem "s 17(1)(p): the date a doctor first physically examined you for the injury, the date the certifying doctor first did, and the certifying doctor's unique identifier" (`What must my notice of claim include` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)))
#ASSERT elem "s 17(2)(b): an offer of settlement (the amount you would accept in full satisfaction), or why you cannot yet make one" (`What must my notice of claim include` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT elem "s 19: written permission for the insurer to have access to, and copy, records about you relevant to the claim held by the bodies s 19 lists" (`What must my notice of claim include` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `s 18 -- what must accompany the notice`

-- Own claim, 30, holds a driver licence (government, photograph), law practice retained: doctor's certificate,
-- claimant's certificate, the (2)(c) statement, certified copy of identity document = 4.
#ASSERT count (`What must go with my notice of claim` FALSE FALSE 30 TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT elem "s 18(4)(a): a certified copy of your current identity document" (`What must go with my notice of claim` FALSE FALSE 30 TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Dependants of a person who died, claimant 14, no law practice: death certificate and claimant's certificate = 2; no
-- identity evidence (under 15).
#ASSERT count (`What must go with my notice of claim` TRUE TRUE 14 TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT elem "s 18(1)(b): a copy of the death certificate" (`What must go with my notice of claim` TRUE TRUE 14 TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Age edge: own claim, no law practice, holds an identity document. At 15: doctor's certificate, claimant's
-- certificate, certified copy = 3. At 14: 2.
#ASSERT count (`What must go with my notice of claim` FALSE FALSE 15 TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT count (`What must go with my notice of claim` FALSE FALSE 14 TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS 2
-- A spouse's claim for loss of consortium (derivative, nobody died), 40, whose government document has no photograph
-- (so is not an identity document): neither s 18(1)(a) nor (b) applies -- no medical certificate at all (finding 1);
-- claimant's certificate and a recent certified photograph = 2.
#ASSERT count (`What must go with my notice of claim` TRUE FALSE 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT elem "s 18(4)(b): a recent certified photograph of you" (`What must go with my notice of claim` TRUE FALSE 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT (NOT (elem "s 18(1)(b): a copy of the death certificate" (`What must go with my notice of claim` TRUE FALSE 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE)))

§§ `s 16 -- form of the notice`

-- (a), (b) met; the form needs no oath: meets s 16.
#ASSERT `Is my notice in the required form` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- The form needs an oath and it is completed: meets s 16.
#ASSERT `Is my notice in the required form` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- The form needs an oath, not completed: fails (c).
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is my notice in the required form` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
-- Not the approved form: fails (a).
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is my notice in the required form` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- Not witnessed: fails (b).
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is my notice in the required form` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))

§§ `s 17(3) -- significant disability`

-- 4 weeks = 28 days. 27 days, not relevant to the assessment: not significant.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is my disability significant` FALSE 27))
-- 28 days: significant ("4 weeks or more").
#ASSERT `Is my disability significant` FALSE 28
-- Relevant to the assessment, however short: significant.
#ASSERT `Is my disability significant` TRUE 0

§§ `s 18(4) and (5) -- identity evidence`

-- Under 15: s 18(4) does not apply.
#ASSERT `Does my identity evidence meet s 18(4)` 14 TRUE TRUE TRUE `a justice of the peace` FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 11 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2026) EQUALS `s 18(4) does not apply: the claimant is under 15`
-- 15, a current driver licence, copy certified by a justice of the peace: met under (a).
#ASSERT `Does my identity evidence meet s 18(4)` 15 TRUE TRUE TRUE `a justice of the peace` FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 11 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2026) EQUALS `met: a certified copy of the claimant's current identity document (s 18(4)(a))`
-- Each listed certifier counts.
#ASSERT `Does my identity evidence meet s 18(4)` 30 TRUE TRUE TRUE `a lawyer` FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 11 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2026) EQUALS `met: a certified copy of the claimant's current identity document (s 18(4)(a))`
#ASSERT `Does my identity evidence meet s 18(4)` 30 TRUE TRUE TRUE `a notary public` FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 11 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2026) EQUALS `met: a certified copy of the claimant's current identity document (s 18(4)(a))`
#ASSERT `Does my identity evidence meet s 18(4)` 30 TRUE TRUE TRUE `a commissioner for declarations` FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 11 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2026) EQUALS `met: a certified copy of the claimant's current identity document (s 18(4)(a))`
-- Certified by a pharmacist (not on the s 18(5) list): not met.
#ASSERT `Does my identity evidence meet s 18(4)` 30 TRUE TRUE TRUE `someone else, or nobody` FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 11 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2026) EQUALS `not met: the copy is not certified by a lawyer, notary public, commissioner for declarations or justice of the peace (s 18(5))`
-- Finding 2: an expired passport, the only identity document held. It is an identity document (s 18(5) says nothing of
-- currency), so (b) is closed, and it is not current, so (a) is closed -- even with a good photograph.
#ASSERT `Does my identity evidence meet s 18(4)` 30 TRUE TRUE FALSE `a justice of the peace` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 11 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2026) EQUALS `not met: the claimant's identity document is not current, and s 18(4)(b) is open only to a claimant who holds no identity document`
-- No identity document (a government card without a photograph). Passport-size photograph taken 7 November 2024,
-- notice 7 November 2026: 24 months before is 7 November 2024, so taken "within the last 2 years" (the edge counts).
-- Certifier has known the claimant since 1 January 2020, certified 1 November 2026: met under (b).
#ASSERT `Does my identity evidence meet s 18(4)` 30 TRUE FALSE FALSE `someone else, or nobody` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 11 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 11 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2026) EQUALS `met: a recent certified photograph, as the claimant holds no identity document (s 18(4)(b))`
-- Taken 6 November 2024: a day too old.
#ASSERT `Does my identity evidence meet s 18(4)` 30 TRUE FALSE FALSE `someone else, or nobody` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 6 11 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 11 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2026) EQUALS `not met: the photograph is not a recent certified photograph (s 18(5))`
-- Not passport-size.
#ASSERT `Does my identity evidence meet s 18(4)` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE `someone else, or nobody` FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 11 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 11 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2026) EQUALS `not met: the photograph is not a recent certified photograph (s 18(5))`
-- Certifier known the claimant since 1 November 2025, certified 1 November 2026: exactly 1 year, "at least 1 year": met.
#ASSERT `Does my identity evidence meet s 18(4)` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE `someone else, or nobody` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 11 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 11 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2026) EQUALS `met: a recent certified photograph, as the claimant holds no identity document (s 18(4)(b))`
-- Known since 2 November 2025: one day short of a year: not met.
#ASSERT `Does my identity evidence meet s 18(4)` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE `someone else, or nobody` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 11 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 11 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 11 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2026) EQUALS `not met: the photograph is not a recent certified photograph (s 18(5))`
-- Leap day: notice 29 February 2028; 24 months before is February 2026, which has no 29th, so 28 February 2026.
-- Taken 28 February 2026: met. Taken 27 February 2026: not met.
#ASSERT `Does my identity evidence meet s 18(4)` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE `someone else, or nobody` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2028) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020) (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 2 2028) EQUALS `met: a recent certified photograph, as the claimant holds no identity document (s 18(4)(b))`
#ASSERT `Does my identity evidence meet s 18(4)` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE `someone else, or nobody` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 27 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2028) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020) (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 2 2028) EQUALS `not met: the photograph is not a recent certified photograph (s 18(5))`
-- Under the core definition directly: a passport-size photograph taken after the notice is given is not "taken within
-- the last 2 years" before it (READING).
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a recent certified photograph (s 18(5))` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 8 11 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 11 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020) (DATE_FROM_DMY 8 11 2026)))
-- s 18(5) identity document: a government document with a photograph.
#ASSERT `is an identity document (s 18(5))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`is an identity document (s 18(5))` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`is an identity document (s 18(5))` FALSE TRUE))

§§ `s 18(5) -- consideration for a referral`

-- Money of any amount is consideration (the exception is for "a gift, other than money").
#ASSERT `Is the referral benefit consideration` `money` 50
-- A $200 bottle of wine: a gift other than money worth $200 or less: not consideration.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is the referral benefit consideration` `a gift other than money` 200))
-- $200.01: consideration.
#ASSERT `Is the referral benefit consideration` `a gift other than money` 200.01
-- A $150 dinner: hospitality of $200 or less: not consideration. $250: consideration.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is the referral benefit consideration` `hospitality` 150))
#ASSERT `Is the referral benefit consideration` `hospitality` 250
-- Any other fee or benefit, however small: consideration.
#ASSERT `Is the referral benefit consideration` `another fee or benefit` 10

§§ `s 20 -- settlement`

-- s 20(1): unrepresented: the offer must come with the explanatory statement; represented: s 20(1) does not require it.
#ASSERT `Must the offer come with an explanatory statement` FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Must the offer come with an explanatory statement` TRUE))
-- s 20(2): an adult of full capacity: not restricted.
#ASSERT `Can my claim be settled` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 20(2) does not restrict it: the claimant is an adult of full capacity`
-- A 16-year-old, nothing approved: no.
#ASSERT `Can my claim be settled` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: until the court or the public trustee is satisfied it is in the claimant's best interests and approves the terms (s 20(2))`
-- A 16-year-old, the public trustee satisfied and approving: yes.
#ASSERT `Can my claim be settled` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the court or the public trustee is satisfied it is in the claimant's best interests and has approved the terms (s 20(2))`
-- An adult without full capacity, the court satisfied but terms not yet approved: both (a) and (b) are needed: no.
#ASSERT `Can my claim be settled` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: until the court or the public trustee is satisfied it is in the claimant's best interests and approves the terms (s 20(2))`
-- s 20(3): an adult with none of (a)-(c): the insurer may assume full capacity.
#ASSERT `May the insurer assume I have full capacity` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the insurer may assume I am of full capacity (s 20(3))`
-- Each "unless" limb defeats the assumption.
#ASSERT `May the insurer assume I have full capacity` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the insurer may not assume I am of full capacity (s 20(3))`
#ASSERT `May the insurer assume I have full capacity` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the insurer may not assume I am of full capacity (s 20(3))`
#ASSERT `May the insurer assume I have full capacity` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the insurer may not assume I am of full capacity (s 20(3))`
-- A child claimant: s 20(3) speaks only of adults.
#ASSERT `May the insurer assume I have full capacity` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 20(3) does not say: it is about adult claimants only`
-- s 20(4): an application and (a): the court may declare. An application and (b): may. No application: may not.
-- An application but neither ground: may not.
#ASSERT `Can the court put me under its protection` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the court put me under its protection` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Can the court put me under its protection` FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Can the court put me under its protection` TRUE FALSE FALSE))

§§ `s 21 -- expenses`

-- Medical expenses of exactly $200 with receipts: "at least $200": meets s 21.
#ASSERT `Does my expenses request meet s 21` `private hospital, medical and pharmaceutical expenses (Act, s 42)` 200 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: my request meets s 21`
-- $199.99 with receipts, more requests to come: below $200: does not meet s 21.
#ASSERT `Does my expenses request meet s 21` `private hospital, medical and pharmaceutical expenses (Act, s 42)` 199.99 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: my request does not meet s 21`
-- $150, the last request, for the whole outstanding total, with receipts: s 21(2) lets it through.
#ASSERT `Does my expenses request meet s 21` `private hospital, medical and pharmaceutical expenses (Act, s 42)` 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: my request meets s 21`
-- $150, the last request, but not for the whole outstanding total: s 21(2) does not apply.
#ASSERT `Does my expenses request meet s 21` `private hospital, medical and pharmaceutical expenses (Act, s 42)` 150 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: my request does not meet s 21`
-- $150, the last request, whole total, but no evidence: s 21(1)(b) still applies.
#ASSERT `Does my expenses request meet s 21` `private hospital, medical and pharmaceutical expenses (Act, s 42)` 150 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: my request does not meet s 21`
-- Rehabilitation expenses of $500 with evidence: meets; without evidence: does not.
#ASSERT `Does my expenses request meet s 21` `rehabilitation expenses (Act, s 51)` 500 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: my request meets s 21`
#ASSERT `Does my expenses request meet s 21` `rehabilitation expenses (Act, s 51)` 500 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: my request does not meet s 21`
-- Lost wages: not expenses s 21 covers.
#ASSERT `Does my expenses request meet s 21` `other expenses` 500 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 21 does not say: it covers only private hospital, medical, pharmaceutical and rehabilitation expenses`

§§ `s 22 -- information the insurer obtains`

-- Obtained 31 January 2026: "within 1 month after" ends 28 February 2026 (February has no 31st).
#ASSERT `the last day to give the claimant the information (s 22(1))` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 1 2026) EQUALS (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2026)
-- Obtained 15 June 2026: last day 15 July 2026.
#ASSERT `the last day to give the claimant the information (s 22(1))` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 6 2026) EQUALS (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 7 2026)
-- Received on the last day, 28 February 2026: in time.
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer give me the information` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 1 2026) FALSE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 3 2026) EQUALS `the insurer gave me the information in time (s 22(1))`
-- Received 1 March 2026: late; the last day was 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer give me the information` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 1 2026) FALSE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 3 2026) EQUALS `the insurer is late: the last day was` (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2026)
-- Not received, today 28 February 2026: the insurer still has until today.
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer give me the information` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 1 2026) FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2026) EQUALS `the insurer has until this day to give me the information (s 22(1))` (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2026)
-- Not received, today 1 March 2026: late.
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer give me the information` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 1 2026) FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) EQUALS `the insurer is late: the last day was` (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2026)
-- Received 15 July 2026 for information obtained 15 June 2026: in time.
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer give me the information` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 6 2026) FALSE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 7 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 7 2026) EQUALS `the insurer gave me the information in time (s 22(1))`
-- The insurer says it withholds on suspicion of fraud: s 22(2)-(3).
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer give me the information` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 1 2026) TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) EQUALS `the insurer may withhold it if it has reasonable grounds to suspect me of fraud, and must then tell the commission within 1 month (s 22(2)-(3))`

-- The regulative rule in the core, on the 31 January 2026 facts (28 days to 28 February). Day 0 is 31 January.
GIVEN `the day given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 22 trace is fulfilled when the information is given on day` `the day given` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 22 -- the insurer must give the claimant the information within 1 month, unless it withholds it on suspicion of fraud` 28) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `give the claimant the information` `the day given`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the day of the decision` IS A NUMBER
      `the days left`           IS A NUMBER
      `the day told`            IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 22 trace is fulfilled when withheld on day` `the day of the decision` `with` `the days left` `days left and the commission told on day` `the day told` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 22 -- the insurer must give the claimant the information within 1 month, unless it withholds it on suspicion of fraud` 28) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` (`decide to withhold the information` `the days left`) `the day of the decision`), (EVENT `the insurer` `inform the commission of the decision and its grounds` `the day told`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Given on day 28 (28 February): fulfilled. On day 29 (1 March): not.
#ASSERT `the s 22 trace is fulfilled when the information is given on day` 28
#ASSERT (NOT (`the s 22 trace is fulfilled when the information is given on day` 29))
-- Withheld on day 10 (10 February; 1 month after is 10 March, 28 days on), the commission told on day 38 (10 March):
-- fulfilled. Told on day 39: not.
#ASSERT `the s 22 trace is fulfilled when withheld on day` 10 `with` 28 `days left and the commission told on day` 38
#ASSERT (NOT (`the s 22 trace is fulfilled when withheld on day` 10 `with` 28 `days left and the commission told on day` 39))
-- Decided to withhold on day 29, after the month had run: too late to take the s 22(2) way out; not fulfilled.
#ASSERT (NOT (`the s 22 trace is fulfilled when withheld on day` 29 `with` 31 `days left and the commission told on day` 30))

-- expect: BREACH by the insurer, "s 22(1): the information was not given ... within 1 month" (and the withholding
-- branch breached too).
#TRACE `s 22 -- the insurer must give the claimant the information within 1 month, unless it withholds it on suspicion of fraud` 28 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the claimant` DOES `ask about the information` AT 40

-- expect: BREACH by the insurer, "s 22(3): the commission was not told of the decision to withhold within 1 month
-- after it".
#TRACE `s 22 -- the insurer must give the claimant the information within 1 month, unless it withholds it on suspicion of fraud` 28 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insurer` DOES `decide to withhold the information` 28 AT 10
    PARTY `the claimant` DOES `ask about the information` AT 60

§§ `s 29 -- costs on an accepted mandatory final offer`

-- s 29(1)(c) rates: 30 minutes = 175 x 30/60 = 87.50; 60 minutes = 175; 61 minutes = 175 + 150 x 1/60 = 177.50;
-- 90 minutes = 175 + 75 = 250; 0 minutes = 0.
#ASSERT `the conference representation costs (s 29(1)(c))` 30 EQUALS 87.5
#ASSERT `the conference representation costs (s 29(1)(c))` 60 EQUALS 175
#ASSERT `the conference representation costs (s 29(1)(c))` 61 EQUALS 177.5
#ASSERT `the conference representation costs (s 29(1)(c))` 90 EQUALS 250
#ASSERT `the conference representation costs (s 29(1)(c))` 0 EQUALS 0
-- Offer $40,000 accepted (limits $30,000 and $50,000, HYPOTHETICAL); item 1 $1,000 (100% = 1,000); item 5 $800 (50% =
-- 400); 90 minutes at the conference (250); court application $500 (capped at 400); disbursements $300.
-- 1,000 + 400 + 250 + 400 + 300 = 2,350, under the $3,500 declared costs limit.
#ASSERT `What costs do I get on accepting a mandatory final offer` 40000 TRUE 30000 50000 3500 1000 800 90 500 300 EQUALS `I am entitled to costs of (s 29)` 2350
-- Court application of $399: not capped. 1,000 + 400 + 250 + 399 + 300 = 2,349.
#ASSERT `What costs do I get on accepting a mandatory final offer` 40000 TRUE 30000 50000 3500 1000 800 90 399 300 EQUALS `I am entitled to costs of (s 29)` 2349
-- Declared costs limit $2,000: limited to 2,000 (s 29(2)). Limit $2,350, equal to the amount: 2,350.
#ASSERT `What costs do I get on accepting a mandatory final offer` 40000 TRUE 30000 50000 2000 1000 800 90 500 300 EQUALS `I am entitled to costs of (s 29)` 2000
#ASSERT `What costs do I get on accepting a mandatory final offer` 40000 TRUE 30000 50000 2350 1000 800 90 500 300 EQUALS `I am entitled to costs of (s 29)` 2350
-- No lawyer at the conference, no application, no disbursements: 1,000 + 400 = 1,400.
#ASSERT `What costs do I get on accepting a mandatory final offer` 40000 TRUE 30000 50000 3500 1000 800 0 0 0 EQUALS `I am entitled to costs of (s 29)` 1400
-- Band edges: an offer equal to the lower offer limit is not "more than" it: s 29 does not set the costs. A cent over:
-- it does. Equal to the upper offer limit: it does. A cent over: it does not.
#ASSERT `What costs do I get on accepting a mandatory final offer` 30000 TRUE 30000 50000 3500 1000 800 90 500 300 EQUALS `s 29 does not set my costs: the offer was not accepted, or was not more than the lower offer limit, or was more than the upper offer limit`
#ASSERT `What costs do I get on accepting a mandatory final offer` 30000.01 TRUE 30000 50000 3500 1000 800 90 500 300 EQUALS `I am entitled to costs of (s 29)` 2350
#ASSERT `What costs do I get on accepting a mandatory final offer` 50000 TRUE 30000 50000 3500 1000 800 90 500 300 EQUALS `I am entitled to costs of (s 29)` 2350
#ASSERT `What costs do I get on accepting a mandatory final offer` 50000.01 TRUE 30000 50000 3500 1000 800 90 500 300 EQUALS `s 29 does not set my costs: the offer was not accepted, or was not more than the lower offer limit, or was more than the upper offer limit`
-- Not accepted.
#ASSERT `What costs do I get on accepting a mandatory final offer` 40000 FALSE 30000 50000 3500 1000 800 90 500 300 EQUALS `s 29 does not set my costs: the offer was not accepted, or was not more than the lower offer limit, or was more than the upper offer limit`

§§ `s 30 -- examination allowances`

#ASSERT `Am I entitled to examination allowances` TRUE EQUALS `yes: allowances and expenses on the same basis as a District Court witness (s 30)`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to examination allowances` FALSE EQUALS `s 30 does not say: it covers only a person required to attend for examination under Part 5B of the Act`
